      <ArticleTitle>Whole-pelvic Versus Prostate-only Radiotherapy in Clinically Node-negative High-Risk Localised Prostate Cancer: A Systematic Review and Meta-analysis with Reconstructed Individual-patient Data.</ArticleTitle>
      <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.clon.2026.104329</ELocationID>
      <Abstract>
        <AbstractText Label="AIMS" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">Whether elective whole-pelvic radiotherapy improves outcomes over prostate-only radiotherapy remains an open question.</AbstractText>
        <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Four trials (n=2,500). Pooled HR for overall survival 0.97 (95% CI 0.85-1.10).</AbstractText>
        <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">No survival benefit was observed.</AbstractText>
      </Abstract>
